---
import SectionLabel from "./SectionLabel.astro";
---

<section id="about" class="border-t border-border/60 py-24">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <SectionLabel section="cat about.md" title="A little about me" />

        <div class="mt-14 flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-10">
            <div
                class="relative aspect-4/3 w-full max-w-lg max-h-full mx-auto overflow-hidden border border-border bg-secondary/20 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"
            >
                <div
                    class="absolute inset-4 border border-dashed border-primary/40"
                >
                </div>
                <span class="absolute left-3 top-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 bg-primary"
                ></span>
                <span class="absolute right-3 bottom-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 bg-primary"
                ></span>

                <img
                    src="images/profile_pic.webp"
                    alt="Profile picture"
                    class="absolute border border-primary inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover"
                />
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-8 lg:pt-2">
                <span
                    class="max-w-2xl text-pretty text-xl text-foreground leading-relaxed font-mono font-bold"
                >
                    I started building interfaces.<br />
                    Now, I'm learning about what happens when the request leaves the
                    browser.
                </span>
                <div
                    class="max-w-2xl space-y-5 text-pretty text-md text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed font-mono"
                >
                    <p>
                        My day-to-day work is at a <span
                            class="font-bold text-foreground">Salesforce</span
                        > company, where I help build and improve web platforms around
                        the Salesforce ecosystem. It's a space that keeps me close
                        to both <span class="font-bold text-foreground"
                            >product thinking</span
                        > and the <span class="font-bold text-foreground"
                            >practical details</span
                        > of reliable software.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Outside work, I <span class="font-bold text-foreground"
                            >follow those details</span
                        > deeper: learning how networks move information, how systems
                        behave under preasure, and how engineering connects the two.
                        I enjoy when I can turn a question into a <span
                            class="font-bold text-foreground"
                            >small project</span
                        > and leave with a better mental model.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
